   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`fieldnotes delete INDEX` now works, and `python tools/check.py` passes (5 tests OK, line-length check clean).\n\n**Red:** I added tests before any implementation. The first run failed with 2 errors and 1 failure. Both errors were `AttributeError: module 'fieldnotes.store' has no attribute 'delete'`. The failure was `test_delete_command` getting exit code 2 instead of 0, because the CLI didn't know `delete`.\n\n**Green:**\n- **`fieldnotes/store.py`:** `delete(index)` removes and returns the note at that position. It raises `IndexError` if the index is out of range, and it leaves the file untouched in that case.\n- **`fieldnotes/cli.py`:**\n  - `delete INDEX` prints `deleted: <text>` and exits 0.\n  - A non-integer or out-of-range index prints an error to stderr and exits 2.\n  - I pulled the usage string into a `USAGE` constant that now mentions `delete`.\n- **`tests/test_store.py`:** tests cover a valid delete, out-of-range indexes (0, 2 and -1), the CLI success path, and CLI bad input (`5`, `x` and a missing argument).\n\n- **1-based indexing:** I made INDEX 1-based, in the order `list` prints notes. `list` doesn't print numbers, so users have to count lines. Showing the index in `list` would fix that, but I held off because you didn't ask for it. I can add it, or switch to 0-based, if you prefer.\n- **`NOTES_HOME`:** `tools/check.py` requires `NOTES_HOME`, so I ran it with a temporary directory outside the project.",
   "suspended": false
